      "message": "Keystone does not listen to notifications at this point on the wire, and I\u0027d like to avoid doing that. I am unsure how to handle this however, short of doing a periodic cache+reload of the config.\n\nSo lets think very clearly about how we communicate this across processes without notifying to the wire and hoping that a fanout catches all keystone workers.\n\nOptions that come to mind:\n\n1. Timed cache, when you load the config you look at when it was last updated and check in at a fixed interval (meaning that any/all requests would be updated at the same time, vs. some threads/workers do not update at the same time).\n\n2. Keep an identifier for the \"version\" of the config that is handled via a light-weight query. if the version does not match in-memory state, you reload config.\n\n3. Simple timed cache, knowing that we reload at x interval, so changes need to either be a restart of keystone or wait for interval X to fully apply.\n\n4. ???",
